{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01H1ENGyDniu7pNDPfLJSJcN", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/21/172.867\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-21/chapter-I/subchapter-B/part-172/subpart-I/section-172.867\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CFR-2016-title21-vol3/pdf/CFR-2016-title21-vol3-sec172-869.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2003-08-05/pdf/03-19508.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://regulations.vlex.com/vid/separate-parts-this-issue-iii-human-22745222\"}, {\"url\": \"https://corpora.tika.apache.org/base/docs/govdocs1/320/320464.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://corpora.tika.apache.org/base/docs/govdocs1/320/320455.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.wikipedia.com/wiki/Olestra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2003-10-07/pdf/C3-19509.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www1.udel.edu/chem/C465/senior/fall98/Olestra2/!CONS.HTM\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:14:16.764Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "21 CFR 172.867 olestra vitamins A D E K added", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01EyUTWonNRoyxEid19oWwB3", "content": [{"title": "www.law.cornell.edu", "url": "https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/21/172.867"}, {"title": "Site Feedback", "url": "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-21/chapter-I/subchapter-B/part-172/subpart-I/section-172.867"}, {"title": "CFR 2016 title21 vol3 sec172 869", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CFR-2016-title21-vol3/pdf/CFR-2016-title21-vol3-sec172-869.pdf"}, {"title": "www.govinfo.gov", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2003-08-05/pdf/03-19508.pdf"}, {"title": "Separate Parts In This Issue Part III Health and Human Services Department, Food and Drug Administration,", "url": "https://regulations.vlex.com/vid/separate-parts-this-issue-iii-human-22745222"}, {"title": "[Federal Register: August 5, 2003 (Volume 68, Number 150)]", "url": "https://corpora.tika.apache.org/base/docs/govdocs1/320/320464.html"}, {"title": "corpora.tika.apache.org", "url": "https://corpora.tika.apache.org/base/docs/govdocs1/320/320455.pdf"}, {"title": "www.wikipedia.com", "url": "https://www.wikipedia.com/wiki/Olestra"}, {"title": "C3 19509", "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2003-10-07/pdf/C3-19509.pdf"}, {"title": "www1.udel.edu", "url": "https://www1.udel.edu/chem/C465/senior/fall98/Olestra2/!CONS.HTM"}]}, "The search turned up the regulation's text and its history. Under 21 CFR 172.867, olestra-containing foods must be fortified with fixed amounts of fat-soluble vitamins to offset olestra's effect on their absorption. The regulation sets 1.9 mg alpha-tocopherol equivalents (vitamin E), 51 retinol equivalents (vitamin A), 12 IU of vitamin D, and 8 µg of vitamin K1, each per gram of olestra. The vitamins were added to compensate for interference with absorption of fat-soluble vitamins.\n\nLabeling is the other key requirement. The four vitamins must appear in the ingredient list, each marked with an asterisk, and they are not counted toward nutrient content on the nutrition label or in any nutrient claims. The asterisk refers to a \"Dietarily insignificant\" statement. That labeling is meant to tell consumers that their vitamin status will not change from eating olestra products.\n\nThe label history: a 1996 rule required a warning statement on olestra products. In 2003 FDA removed the requirement for the label statement specifically for savory snack products containing olestra. The vitamin fortification and the asterisk requirement remained in place.\n\nSources: the Cornell LII text of 172.867, the eCFR version (current as of June 2026), the 2003 Federal Register final rule, and the 2003 correction notice. I did not check whether the eCFR text has changed since June 2026."], "durationSeconds": 7.245579292, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01H1ENGyDniu7pNDPfLJSJcN", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgDYpXhmjfdMhGW66g9x7", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**答案：** 维生素 A、D、E、K。依据是美国联邦法规 21 CFR 172.867。\n\n法规要求每克 olestra 补充：\n- 维生素 E：1.9 mg α-生育酚当量\n- 维生素 A：51 视黄醇当量\n- 维生素 D：12 IU\n- 维生素 K₁：8 µg\n\n这几种维生素要写进配料表，各加一个星号。它们不计入营养成分标签，也不能用来做营养声称。\n\n只搜了 1 次。\n\n**依据网址：**\n- [Cornell LII – 21 CFR 172.867](https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/21/172.867)\n- [eCFR – 21 CFR 172.867](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-21/chapter-I/subchapter-B/part-172/subpart-I/section-172.867)\n- [Federal Register 2003-08-05 最终规则](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2003-08-05/pdf/03-19508.pdf)"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1318, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4301, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1318}, "output_tokens": 361, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:14:20.940Z", "request_id": "req_011CgDYpXQemkf1UjKXRkxoG"}
